  "body": "## Cause\nThe completeness guard of \"Pass starts at\" writes a note with `RINGS_FALLBACK`. The op counts that note and posts `Warning::StrategyFallback`. That warning had one fixed text, for the Adaptive plan. A 2D Offset, a 2D Pocket and a 3D pocket (since #3618) reach the guard. These ops do not use Adaptive, but the user saw \"Adaptive fell back to Offset rings\".\n\n## Change\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`: new enum `FallbackCause` (`Adaptive` | `PassStart`). `StrategyFallback` gets `cause` with `#[serde(default)]`. The default is `Adaptive`. Display has one text for each cause.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pass_start.rs`: new constant `PASS_START_FALLBACK_TAIL` = `\"this area in the Auto order instead\"`. `StartSide::fallback_note` ends with it. New `pass_start_fallbacks(notes)` counts a note when it contains `PASS_START_NOTE`, contains `RINGS_FALLBACK` + the tail, and ends with the tail. The match does not read the start of the note, because 3D pocket writes the note as `Z <level>: <note>` (`machining3d/level_side.rs:62-63`). No Adaptive note ends with the tail. `rings_fallbacks` counts the two kinds as before.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: new `pub fn strategy_fallback(&Toolpath) -> Option<Warning>`. The run uses it. The cause comes from the notes, not from the op kind. `PassStart` is set only when each fallback note is a guard note. An Adaptive op on its ring fallback can write an Adaptive note and a guard note, and then the Adaptive cause stays.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs`: no DTO change. The MCP kind stays `strategy_fallback`. The finding DTO is flat and has no field for the cause. The `message` carries the new text.\n- `crates/ui/src/operations.rs`: the test literal gets the new field.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3542-pass-start-fallback-text.md`.\n- A merge of `origin/main` (conflict in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/mod.rs`: the two `pub use` lines are kept).\n\n## Texts\nOld (and unchanged for the Adaptive cause):\n`Adaptive fell back to Offset rings on 1 area from move 0: the notes name each one and why (the post is not held: the rings are verified)`\n\nNew (pass-start cause):\n`Pass starts at: the selected start side would leave material uncut in 1 area, so the Auto order was used there instead, from move 0: the notes name each one (the post is not held: the cut is verified)`\n\n## Pins\n- `offset_pass_start::the_offset_guard_fallback_warning_names_the_pass_start`: exact text of the pass-start case from the 2D Offset guard note. The 3D pocket form (`Z 1.000: <note>`) gives the same warning. A path with an Adaptive note and a guard note keeps the Adaptive cause.\n- `offset_pass_start::a_strategy_fallback_saved_without_a_cause_reads_as_adaptive`: a cache without `cause` reads as `Adaptive`. The serde name `strategy_fallback` does not change. The round trip of `pass_start` is exact.\n- `strategy_fallback::an_adaptive_fallback_to_offset_rings_is_a_warning`: an exact `assert_eq!` of the Adaptive text from a real generation (proves \"unchanged\").\n- `mcp::job::tests::a_pass_start_fallback_keeps_the_strategy_fallback_kind` (app lib): the kind is `strategy_fallback` and advisory for the two causes.\n- `machining2d::pass_start::tests::the_guard_fallback_is_an_offset_rings_fallback` (motion lib): `pass_start_fallbacks` counts the guard note and the `Z 1.000: ` prefixed note. It does not count the two Adaptive note forms. `rings_fallbacks` counts each of them one time.\n\n## Gate (head f9f9cf385, debug, `-j 6`)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim`: all binaries pass.\n- motion `--lib` 548; `pass_start_levels` 7; `pocket3d_pass_start` 2. All pass.\n- app `--lib` 300; `strategy_fallback` 1; `offset_pass_start` 6 (2 ignored heavy); `pocket_pass_start` 6; `adaptive_pass_start` 4; `adaptive_zero_margin_island` 4; `pocket3d_pass_start` 3; `docs_troubleshooting` 1; `mcp_verify` 3; `golden_cl` 33; `conformance` 7; `example_catalog` 37 (4 ignored); `first_part_programs` 2. All pass.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib` 1493 pass.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: sim and motion `--all-targets`, app `--lib` + `offset_pass_start` + `strategy_fallback`, ui `--all-targets`. Clean.\n\n## Not run\n- No heavy lane (P3). No app window.\n- The red-first run of the new Offset text was not shown separately. Before this change the only text was the Adaptive text, so the `assert_eq!` cannot pass on the old code.\n- No fixture hits the guard on a real op. `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_pass_start.rs` has no case that falls back. The tests feed the real guard note (`StartSide::fallback_note`, also in its 3D pocket form) to the same function that the run uses.\n\n## Follow-up\n- #3622 (P7): the area count is not true for 3D pocket levels (one note for each level) and for an Adaptive ring fallback with a guard fallback (two notes for one area). This is the \"Also seen\" item of the issue.\n\nChangelog: The warning after a \"Pass starts at\" fallback (2D Offset, 2D Pocket, 3D pocket) now names the pass start and the Auto order, not the Adaptive strategy.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3542\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
